  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday night through Tuesday)\nIssued at 1203 AM MST Wed Nov 18 2026\n\nSouthwest flow aloft will continue to strengthen Thursday night \ninto Friday as the upper level low opens up and lifts northeast \nfrom the Great Basin across the Rockies. This setup will bring a \ndeeper lee side trough and breezy to windy conditions Friday, with\nspeeds forecast to remain below advisory threshold. The models \nare trending toward a trailing trough moving east across the area \non Saturday, but differ on the amplification and whether a low \nwill close off or not. QPF is trending up for Saturday across \nnorthern NM and snow levels will be much lower than with the \nprevious couple of troughs, but this will be a quick-hitter which\nwill limit amounts to below advisory threshold. Another quick- \nhitting upper level trough is forecast to for Monday into Monday \nnight, bringing a limited round of precipitation. The wave train \nis modeled to persist beyond early next week, but with notable \nspread with regard to amplification. Temperatures will trend down\nSaturday and generally be below average through early next week \ndue to progressively colder troughs moving through the region.",
